# DianaSh golden corpus. Recorded from the C# shell, byte for byte, and frozen since its recorder went with the C# core host on 2026-11-07 - see EmuSen_DianaSh.md §13.4.
# Patterns: <ROOT> is the sandbox's real root, <TEMP> the corpus's real temporary folder, <INSTALL> the install's real directory;
# a 'match' block is a regular expression the whole output must match, written where a line prints a time or a measured number.
command counters
usage 1   counters on <space>           start tallying reads/writes/executes for <space>
usage 2   counters off                  stop tallying (kept counts stay readable)
usage 3   counters clear                zero every count, stay armed
usage 4   counters <addr> [<len>]       totals over a range, default length 1
usage 5   counters top [r|w|x|u] [<n>]  hottest addresses, default reads, default 20
usage 6   counters cold <addr> <len>    addresses in the range nothing ever touched

case with no target
target none
covers 1
$ counters
out 58
No ROM loaded - this command needs an active debug target.
status 1
action none
$ echo $?
out 1
1
status 0
action none
end

